Cross-Platform UI Toolkit

-> You are developing a UI library that supports both Windows and macOS.
   You need to render different UI components (Buttons, Checkboxes, and
   TextFields). A Windows button looks and behaves differently than a
   macOS button. If a user sets their app to "Windows mode," the app must
   ensure it only spawns Windows-style components, never mixing them up
   with macOS ones.

-> Task: Create a system that produces families of related objects.
1. Create interfaces for the products: Button and Checkbox.
2. Create concrete families: WinButton/WinCheckbox and MacButton/MacCheckbox.
3. Create an UIFactory interface with createButton() and createCheckbox() methods.
4. Implement WinUIFactory and MacUIFactory to output their respective components.